{
  "id": "state-space",
  "term": "state space",
  "definition": "In this social-processes context, a state space is a way of representing the moment-to-moment relation between two time-synchronized categorical variables so that changes in an interaction system can be visualized over time. It helps researchers examine the emerging structure and dynamic properties of social or team processes.",
